<title>BELGIUM: EU clears venture in infrared technology.</title>
<headline>EU clears venture in infrared technology.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it had cleared a joint venture resulting from the acquisition of half of the capital of AEG Infrarot-module by Bodenseewerk Geraetetechnik GmbH. The other 50 percent of the capital will continue to be held by EHG Elektroholding which previously held full control of the company.</p>
<p>AEG Infrarot, which is active in military technology, the only German manufacturer of key components in the field of infra-red technology which is used in the manufacture of thermal imaging devices and infra-red devices for military missiles. The Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
